  "claims": [
    "Every primitive in the concrete completed MAC/structure catalogue has a typed six-form RootView. Every competitor inside an association source has a typed eight-form AssocCase: same association, left-root crypto/association/seq-fusion/suffix, change in first/middle/last argument.",
    "Primitive competitors are exhaustively classified for all six source kinds: crypto has one form, association eight, wire one opaque pure-wire competitor form, sequential fusion three, tensor fusion three, suffix two. Thus the rooted mixed circuit-level cases have eighteen parameterized forms.",
    "classifyBranch is a total executable recursion on two actual steps. It returns a typed root case, a separated witness, or a recursive common placement. classification_total proves an indexed witness exists for every pair. Recursion depth is bounded by each original mixed step-position length.",
    "The root wire case intentionally retains two actual pure-wire edits without classifying their internal overlaps. Eighteen tags do not imply a complete finite pure-wire or mixed higher basis.",
    "The association/nested-suffix higher square is derived using the existing suffix definition twice, association naturality, pentagon, contextual placement, and proof-groupoid rotation. No new generator or arbitrary parallel-path oracle is added.",
    "For every stage n and typed continuations T and R, suffixAssocCell compares the two-step suffix-first route to the three-step association-first route. Its support is exactly ({n,n+1} union T.needs) union R.needs and its Four-constructor count is fifty-one.",
    "The derived square has exact fresh-condition distribution and repaired joint kernel equality retaining arbitrary correlated past and original input, assuming an updated checked old-catalogue model, cached conditions and transfer/rechecking as stated.",
    "The current completed catalogue is not forward confluent: association versus sequential-wire fusion reaches distinct irreducible endpoints after two and one steps respectively, for every stage. fusion_kernel_equal nevertheless proves the endpoint kernels equal for every compatible box model and input."
  ],
