  "limits": [
    "Classification does not itself produce joining paths or higher filling cells for every case. A verified dispatcher from all classified cases to a uniform filling output is not supplied.",
    "Pure-wire internal critical overlaps remain opaque. The eleven pure-wire equation forms are not proved a complete presentation. A finite list of parameterized mixed forms is not a finite list of all ground typed cells.",
    "Association against sequential-wire-fusion remains an obstruction to forward confluence in this exact catalogue. Further mixed structural rules, a different presentation, or a coherence argument modulo association may resolve it; the negative theorem is not an impossibility result for all presentations.",
    "The association/nested-suffix case is now filled by an explicit derivation from existing diagrams. Full global coherence, a complete finite mixed homotopy basis, and a general convergence strategy are still unproved.",
    "The fifty-one count measures only the produced Four syntax constructors, excluding tracks, circuit/wire/context/guard payloads and shared libraries. The classification depth bound is not a runtime, total size or pure-wire complexity bound.",
    "Formal path rotation reverses equality-preserving rewrite proofs, not stochastic execution or a shared probabilistic continuation. Repair compares circuits in the same updated model, not old and updated model distributions.",
    "The existing MAC semantics, full state/trace and conditions remain unchanged. No new cryptographic bound, computational reduction implementation, continuing native-machine contract, independent ordinary comparison, or dimension-exclusive complexity advantage is proved."
  ],
